<h1><span lang="EN-US">Auto Extract Sphere</span></h1>
<div class="Normal" style="margin:0cm; margin-bottom:.0001pt;">
<hr align="center" size="5" width="100%" class="whs3"></div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="path" lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Datuming</b></span><span class="path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&gt;</b></span> <span class="path" lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Auto Extract</b></span><span class="path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&gt;</b></span> <span class="path" lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Sphere</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <span class="shortcut" lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + A</b></span><span class="shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>lt +</b></span> <span class="shortcut" lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>4</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="command" lang="EN-US">Auto Extract Sphere</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command fits and creates datum spheres to the visible mesh selections. This command is grayed if there is no mesh selection or all selections are hidden.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">The shape proximity is compared to all entity points, which is very useful for imported IGES files.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Call the</span> <span class="command"><span lang="EN-US">Auto Extract Plane</span></span> <span lang="EN-GB">command and the following dialog will appear:</span></p>
<p><img src="../images/auto_sphere.jpg" width="257px" height="165px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US">Acceptance RMS</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">RMS threshold when fitting sphere. Decrease this value to extract spheres from more spherical-shaped objects and vice versa. Default value is 0.01mm.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-underline:none; text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP168464267" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/image027.jpg" width="604px" height="458px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></span></p>
</div>
<p><span class="command">Auto Extract <span lang="EN-US">Sphere</span></span> <span lang="EN-GB">could be useful for finding the radius (by fitting a sphere) of a hemisphere or spherical segment.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Use</span></b> <span class="command"><span lang="EN-US">Auto Extract Sphere</span></span> <span lang="EN-GB">to extract all spheres from all mesh selections at once. It is very useful when import IGES files into KUBE.</span></p>
